{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - User - Session - Okta User Session Impersonation",
	"Description": "An Okta administrator started, extended, or was granted an impersonation session. Impersonation lets an admin act as another user, and everything done inside the session is attributed to the impersonated account, so this is both a legitimate support tool and a very clean way to act as someone else.\n\nEvent types: user.session.impersonation.initiate, user.session.impersonation.grant, user.session.impersonation.extend, user.session.impersonation.revoke, user.session.impersonation.end\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/sigmahq/sigma/identity/okta/okta_user_session_impersonation/\n- https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/identity/okta/okta_user_session_impersonation.yml\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "ebe98b3d-141b-5b8b-b003-0f54ae3cea0c",
	"SearchReference": "dc7485cb-e234-5d26-a5e7-261f1b7d8487"
}